    {
      "id": "note-overview",
      "type": "text_bubble",
      "position": {
        "x": 150,
        "y": -340
      },
      "width": 400,
      "height": 400,
      "style": {
        "width": 400,
        "height": 400
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Note",
        "title": "CHILLED WATER CIRCUIT",
        "text": "Demonstrates a closed-loop industrial chilled water cooling circuit with parallel primary pumps, check valve protection, heat exchanger cooling load, dynamic 3-way TCV mixing, and an expansion reservoir.\n\nAfter running, compare the flows of the two pumps, the heat exchanger outlet temperature and the 3-way valve position. Some coil lines run at about 5.6 m/s, above the usual 2 to 3 m/s guideline for liquid lines: the pipe sizes are chosen for demonstration.\n\nInstruments: TIT 101 chilled water supply temperature, PDIT 102 evaporator pressure drop (low = low evaporator flow, freeze risk), FIT 103 cooling coil flow and FIT 104 pump A flow. Solve all cases: a pump trip runs pump A out and starves the evaporator.",
        "fontSize": "md"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "expansion-tank",
      "type": "tank",
      "position": {
        "x": -50,
        "y": 250
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Chilled Water Reservoir",
        "level_m": 3.0,
        "elevation_m": 5.0,
        "temperature_k": 279.15
      }
    },
